---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy & audience measurement — STOA"
  description="How gostoa.dev uses optional Google Analytics and Clarity session replays, remembers your choice and masks contact forms."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-24 pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-8">Privacy &amp; audience measurement</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">Last updated: 10 November 2026</p>

      <div class="prose prose-invert prose-gray max-w-none space-y-8 text-gray-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">1. This website</h2>
          <p>
            CAB Ingénierie maintains the STOA website at <strong>gostoa.dev</strong>.
            This page describes audience measurement and contact information on that website.
            Documentation, the developer portal and the console are separate services; refer to
            their own information for the processing carried out there.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">2. Optional Google Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            Google Analytics 4 helps us understand which pages people visit and whether they follow
            links to documentation, the quickstart or contact options. Its script loads and its
            measurement requests begin only after you accept. You can refuse just as easily as you accept.
          </p>
          <p>
            Once enabled, this service may use analytics cookies and send usage and technical
            information to Google. Advertising storage, advertising user data and personalised
            advertising remain disabled in this integration.
          </p>
          <p>
            The page address and referring address sent by this integration exclude query parameters
            and fragments. The measured link clicks use only the categories documentation, quickstart
            and contact, with cleaned addresses. Link text, message contents and other form entries
            are not included in those events.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">3. Your choice</h2>
          <p>
            Your acceptance or refusal is remembered locally in this browser for six months.
            The persistent settings button on every page lets you change that choice or withdraw
            consent at any time. The same explicit choice controls Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity.
            Withdrawal stops both integrations and removes their accessible analytics cookies from this site.
          </p>
          <p>
            This six-month period applies to your saved choice. It does not specify how long
            Google or Microsoft retains measurement data, and withdrawal does not erase data already sent.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">4. Optional session replays</h2>
          <p>
            With your consent, Microsoft Clarity reconstructs visits to this public website from
            page structure, clicks, scrolling and navigation. These session replays help us find
            navigation difficulties. They do not record your screen as a video and do not cover
            the STOA application, portal or console.
          </p>
          <p>
            Forms and their contents are explicitly masked, and the project uses strict masking.
            Session replay stops as soon as a form field, editable area or embedded form receives
            focus, and remains off until the next page navigation. Visits with query parameters
            or fragments in the page or referring address are excluded from replay at startup.
            We do not send a name, email address or account identifier through Clarity’s identification API.
            Clarity can use its own pseudonymous cookies to link pages in a visit. Page addresses and
            technical interaction data can be transmitted to Microsoft; the URL cleanup described
            for Google Analytics does not apply to Clarity.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">5. Contact information</h2>
          <p>
            When you contact us, we use the information you provide to respond to your request.
            Message contents are not part of the audience-measurement events described above.
            Any separate signup or account service provides its own information at the point of use.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">6. Questions and requests</h2>
          <p>
            For questions about privacy or a request concerning your personal data, contact
            CAB Ingénierie at
            <a href="mailto:privacy@gostoa.dev" class="text-primary-400 hover:text-primary-300">privacy@gostoa.dev</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
